# Tabs in the source and in help text are shown as four spaces.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv'
|	where	amount > 1	AND	amount < 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..52
  PIPELINE@0..51
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 "\t"
    WHERE_OP@20..51
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 "\t"
      BIN_EXPR@26..51
        BIN_EXPR@26..36
          NAME_REF@26..32
            IDENT@26..32 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
          GT@33..34 ">"
          WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
          LITERAL@35..36
            LONG@35..36 "1"
        WHITESPACE@36..37 "\t"
        IDENT@37..40 "AND"
        WHITESPACE@40..41 "\t"
        BIN_EXPR@41..51
          NAME_REF@41..47
            IDENT@41..47 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@47..48 " "
          LT@48..49 "<"
          WHITESPACE@49..50 " "
          LITERAL@50..51
            LONG@50..51 "5"
  WHITESPACE@51..52 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `AND` in capitals
  --> query:2:20
  |
2 | |    where    amount > 1    AND    amount < 5
  |                             ^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: write `and` in lowercase: `amount > 1    and    amount < 5`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv'
    |	where	amount > 1	and	amount < 5
which parses without errors
